<description>
Reflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.

Input structure:
- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel
  separator line in a non-background color.
- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.
- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.

Rule:
- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.
- Mirror each source object across the separator line.
- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the
  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the
  reflected object in the source color.

Key insight:
- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified
  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while
  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "solid rectangular foreground objects all on one side of the full separator row/column",
  "dst": "their mirror positions across the separator line",
  "transform": "copy each source object by reflection; recolor the rectangular strip between each source object and its mirror to the separator color, overwriting background or distractor pixels inside that strip"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-23 rows x 18-23 cols
  colors: exactly 4 distinct — background, separator, source, distractor
  separator:
    one full-span row or column of a single non-bg color (1 px wide)
    position: 35-50% of the grid dimension from one edge
  source_rects:
    count: 2-3 solid rectangles of a single non-bg/non-sep color
    size: each 2-5 rows x 2-4 cols, area > 1
    placement: all strictly on the same side of the separator
    non-overlapping row-ranges (vertical sep) or col-ranges (horizontal sep)
    each reflection must fit within grid bounds on the opposite side
    gap to separator: 2-5 cells [observed]
  distractors:
    single non-bg/non-sep/non-src color scattered on both sides of separator
    mostly isolated pixels with occasional 2-3 px clusters
    density: 3-10% of total cells; not placed on the separator line
  output:
    same grid size; for each source rect, paint its mirror across the separator
    in source color, and fill the rectangular corridor between original and
    mirror (including over the separator column/row) with the separator color;
    distractors inside corridors get overwritten, others preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size, 4 distinct colors (bg, sep, src, dist), separator orientation
    2. Place separator at ~35-50% position along the perpendicular axis
    3. Choose source side; place 2-3 solid rects on that side with non-overlapping
       row/col spans, ensuring each mirror fits on the opposite side
    4. Build the output by reflecting each rect and filling corridors with sep color
    5. Derive input by removing the mirrored rects and corridor fills (restore bg)
    6. Scatter distractor pixels (density 3-10%) on both sides, avoiding the
       separator line; some may land inside future corridor regions
```
